IMPORT prelude

-- Road Traffic Act 1961 (Singapore) -- speeding and what follows it: the offence (s 63), its punishment by the general
-- penalty (s 131(2)), composition and its statutory cap (s 135), compounded offences at sentencing (s 139AA), speeding in the
-- repeat-offender and enhanced-penalty tests (ss 64(11)(b), 67A(2)), the court's power to disqualify and its effect
-- (ss 42, 43(1)), the points system and the Deputy Commissioner of Police's suspension power (ss 45, 46, 47, 47A), revocation
-- of a new driver's licence (s 35A), and the owner's presumption for a specified offence (s 81(1B), Third Schedule Part 1).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 23 September 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/RTA1961.txt.
--
-- WHY. Added on 11 October 2026 for REQ-0273 (Jun Hao scenario, event j084): a motorcyclist caught at 25 km/h over the limit
-- on an expressway -- the composition sum, the demerit points, and when the licence is suspended.
--
-- WHAT THE ACT DOES NOT HOLD. The Act fixes the maximum punishment, the cap on a composition sum, and the machinery of points
-- and suspension. It does NOT fix: the speed limit on an expressway (prescribed under s 63(1) or notified under s 63(2)); which
-- offences are compoundable and for how much (rules under s 135(2)); the points for an offence, the suspension threshold and the
-- period over which it is counted (rules under s 45(2) and (4)); the revocation threshold for a new driver (rules under
-- s 35A(2) and (4)). Those are INPUTS here.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the speed-limit notifications and rules themselves; the composition rules and any published scale; the points
-- rules; s 47C (immediate suspension after an incident under investigation); s 42A (failing to attend court); s 45(9)
-- (suspension pending process of court); s 47B; vocational licences (s 110 and its demerit points); s 133 (traffic ticket
-- notices) beyond a mention; sentencing practice and case law.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Road Traffic Act 1961 -- speeding`

§§ `63 -- the offence`

-- s 63(1): "it is not lawful for any person to drive a motor vehicle of any class or description on a road at a speed greater
-- than any speed which may be prescribed as the maximum speed in relation to a vehicle of that class or description."
-- (2): the Minister may "by notification in the Gazette, prohibit the driving of motor vehicles ... above a specified speed over
-- any specified road". (4): "A person who drives a motor vehicle on a road at a speed exceeding any speed limit imposed by or in
-- exercise of powers conferred by this Act shall be guilty of an offence."
--
-- s 63 names no class of vehicle and no road: a motorcycle and an expressway are reached only through whatever limit has been
-- prescribed or notified. The limit is an input.
GIVEN `the speed limit` IS A NUMBER
      `the speed driven` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the speeding offence is committed` IF
    `the speed driven` GREATER THAN `the speed limit`

GIVEN `the speed limit` IS A NUMBER
      `the speed driven` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the excess over the limit` MEANS
    IF `the speed driven` GREATER THAN `the speed limit` THEN `the speed driven` - `the speed limit` ELSE 0

§§ `131(2) -- the punishment`

-- s 63(4) creates the offence and provides no penalty. s 131(2): any person guilty of an offence under "any other provision of
-- this Act or the rules" is liable, "where no special penalty is provided -- (a) in the case of a first offence -- to a fine not
-- exceeding $1,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 months or to both; and (b) in the case of a second or
-- subsequent offence -- to a fine not exceeding $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both."
--
-- INFERENCE: "second or subsequent offence" is read as a second conviction under s 63(4). The Act does not say whether an earlier
-- offence under another provision counts, nor whether a compounded offence counts (it is not a conviction).
-- There is NO minimum fine and NO speed band: 1 km/h and 60 km/h over carry the same maximum.
GIVEN `has an earlier speeding conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for speeding` MEANS
    IF `has an earlier speeding conviction` THEN 2000 ELSE 1000

GIVEN `has an earlier speeding conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum months of imprisonment for speeding` MEANS
    IF `has an earlier speeding conviction` THEN 6 ELSE 3

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum fine for speeding` MEANS 0

§§ `135 -- composition`

-- s 135(1): "A relevant authorised officer may compound any offence under this Act or the rules that is PRESCRIBED AS A
-- COMPOUNDABLE OFFENCE, by collecting from a person reasonably suspected of having committed the offence a sum not exceeding the
-- lower of the following: (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $5,000."
-- (1A): "On payment of the composition sum ... no further proceedings are to be taken against that person in respect of the
-- offence." (2): "The appropriate Minister may make rules to prescribe the offences that may be compounded under this section".
--
-- So the Act gives a CEILING, not a sum. Whether speeding is compoundable at all, and the sum actually charged, are for the
-- rules under s 135(2) and the published scale.
-- INFERENCE: for s 63(4) the "maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence" is the s 131(2) maximum for a first offence
-- ($1,000) or a second or subsequent offence ($2,000); composition happens before conviction, and the Act does not say which.
-- Either way the $5,000 limb never bites for speeding.
GIVEN `the maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the composition cap for` MEANS
    IF `the maximum fine` / 2 LESS THAN 5000 THEN `the maximum fine` / 2 ELSE 5000

GIVEN `has an earlier speeding conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the composition cap for speeding` MEANS
    `the composition cap for` (`the maximum fine for speeding` `has an earlier speeding conviction`)

GIVEN `the sum demanded` IS A NUMBER
      `has an earlier speeding conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `speeding is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the composition sum is within the Act` IF
        `speeding is prescribed as compoundable`
    AND `the sum demanded` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the sum demanded` AT MOST `the composition cap for speeding` `has an earlier speeding conviction`

-- s 139AA: "a court may take into account, as an aggravating factor, any offence that has been compounded (on or after
-- 1 November 2019) under this Act before the date of the sentencing."
GIVEN `compounded on or after 1 November 2019` IS A BOOLEAN
      `compounded before the sentencing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the compounded offence may aggravate a later sentence` IF
    `compounded on or after 1 November 2019` AND `compounded before the sentencing`

§§ `64(11)(b), 67A(2) -- when speeding counts towards a worse offence`

-- s 64(11)(b) (and s 65(11)(b) in the same words): a person is a REPEAT OFFENDER for dangerous (or careless) driving if "(i) the
-- person has been convicted ... of an offence under section 63(4) on at least 2 other earlier occasions within the period of
-- 5 years immediately before the date on which the person is convicted of the current offence; (ii) in respect of at least 2 of
-- those convictions, the court is satisfied that ... the person had driven ... at a speed which exceeded by more than 40
-- kilometres per hour the speed limit".
GIVEN `earlier speeding convictions within 5 years` IS A NUMBER
      `of which by more than 40 km/h` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `speeding makes a repeat dangerous or careless driver` IF
        `earlier speeding convictions within 5 years` AT LEAST 2
    AND `of which by more than 40 km/h` AT LEAST 2

-- s 67A(1): a person "having been convicted of 2 or more specified offences" who is "again convicted" of one may, if the court
-- thinks it expedient for the protection of the public, be punished up to "3 times the amount of punishment to which he or she
-- would otherwise have been liable ... except that where imprisonment is imposed it shall not exceed 10 years". s 63(4) is a
-- specified offence (s 67A(3)(a)). But (2): "This section does not apply to a person who has been convicted of an offence under
-- section 63(4) unless the court is satisfied that in committing the offence and the offence in respect of which he or she had
-- been previously convicted, he or she had driven ... at a speed which exceeded by more than 40 kilometres per hour".
-- INFERENCE: "the offence in respect of which he or she had been previously convicted" is read as at least one earlier
-- conviction for speeding by more than 40 km/h; the singular sits awkwardly with the "2 or more" of (1).
GIVEN `earlier specified offence convictions` IS A NUMBER
      `the current excess` IS A NUMBER
      `an earlier conviction was for speeding by more than 40 km/h` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the enhanced penalty is open for speeding` IF
        `earlier specified offence convictions` AT LEAST 2
    AND `the current excess` GREATER THAN 40
    AND `an earlier conviction was for speeding by more than 40 km/h`

GIVEN `has an earlier speeding conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the enhanced maximum fine for speeding` MEANS
    3 * `the maximum fine for speeding` `has an earlier speeding conviction`

GIVEN `has an earlier speeding conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the enhanced maximum months for speeding` MEANS
    IF 3 * `the maximum months of imprisonment for speeding` `has an earlier speeding conviction` GREATER THAN 120
    THEN 120
    ELSE 3 * `the maximum months of imprisonment for speeding` `has an earlier speeding conviction`

§§ `42, 43(1) -- disqualification by the court`

-- s 42(1): where a person is convicted of "(a) an offence under this Act or any other written law in connection with the driving
-- of a motor vehicle", "the court may, in addition to imposing on the offender the punishment provided for such offence, make an
-- order disqualifying the offender from holding or obtaining a driving licence for life or for any period that the court thinks
-- fit." (3): the disqualification may be limited to vehicles of the same class.
-- INFERENCE: speeding is "an offence ... in connection with the driving of a motor vehicle".
-- Nothing in the Act makes disqualification for speeding MANDATORY, or sets a minimum period for it.
GIVEN `convicted of speeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may disqualify` IF `convicted of speeding`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the mandatory minimum disqualification months for speeding` MEANS 0

-- s 43(1): the licence of a person disqualified by a conviction or order "(a) is suspended as long as the disqualification
-- continues in force if ... disqualified ... for a period of less than one year; and (b) is of no effect if ... for a period of
-- one year or longer and he or she must not drive a motor vehicle after the period of disqualification unless he or she passes
-- the prescribed test of competence to drive." s 45(6): on such an order "every point awarded against the person ... must
-- thereupon be cancelled."
DECLARE LicenceEffect IS ONE OF
    `suspended for the period`
    `of no effect, and a new test is needed`

GIVEN `months disqualified` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LicenceEffect
`the effect of a court disqualification` MEANS
    IF `months disqualified` LESS THAN 12 THEN `suspended for the period` ELSE `of no effect, and a new test is needed`

GIVEN `disqualified by a court for a specified period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the points are cancelled by the disqualification` IF `disqualified by a court for a specified period`

§§ `45, 46, 47, 47A -- points and suspension by the Deputy Commissioner of Police`

-- s 45(1): the Deputy Commissioner of Police "may suspend a driving licence of a person for a period not exceeding 5 years" if
-- the person's record "establishes that it would not be in the interests of public safety for him or her to hold a valid driving
-- licence". (2): "the Minister may make rules establishing a system of awarding points against a person for the commission of an
-- offence". (3): the Deputy Commissioner may so conclude "if that person is awarded, within a prescribed period, points prescribed
-- for the commission of an offence or offences under this Act that are equal to or in excess of the maximum number of points
-- prescribed (called the suspension threshold)". (4): the rules "must -- (a) specify the number of points to be awarded for an
-- offence ...; (c) specify the suspension threshold, the period over which the suspension threshold is calculated".
--
-- So the points for 25 km/h over, the threshold and the period are ALL in the rules. Reaching the threshold makes suspension
-- available ("may"), not automatic.
GIVEN `points within the prescribed period` IS A NUMBER
      `the suspension threshold` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Deputy Commissioner may suspend on points` IF
    `points within the prescribed period` AT LEAST `the suspension threshold`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum suspension months` MEANS 60

-- s 45(5): "Where the points awarded ... reach 50% of the suspension threshold ..., the Deputy Commissioner of Police must give
-- written notice thereof to the person."
GIVEN `points within the prescribed period` IS A NUMBER
      `the suspension threshold` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a half-threshold warning is due` IF
    2 * `points within the prescribed period` AT LEAST `the suspension threshold`

-- s 45(7): where a licence holder "commits on a single occasion more than one offence ..., points must be awarded against him or
-- her only for the offence ... in respect of which the largest number of points may be awarded".
GIVEN `points for the first offence` IS A NUMBER
      `points for the second offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the points awarded for one occasion` MEANS
    IF `points for the first offence` AT LEAST `points for the second offence`
    THEN `points for the first offence`
    ELSE `points for the second offence`

-- s 46(1): "To suspend a person's driving licence under section 45, the Deputy Commissioner of Police must first give a notice
-- ... (a) stating that [he or she] proposes to suspend the person's driving licence on such date ... being at least 4 weeks after
-- the date of giving the notice". (2)(b): the date may be postponed if the person will attend "a prescribed course on safe
-- driving". Days are counted from an arbitrary origin.
GIVEN `the day the notice is given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the earliest suspension day` MEANS `the day the notice is given` + 28

-- s 47(3): at the end of a suspension, "in the case only of a driving licence suspended under section 45(1), the points awarded
-- against him or her must be cancelled." s 47A: a licence suspended under s 45 "for a period of one year or any other longer
-- period has no effect and the holder ... must not drive ... after the period of suspension unless he or she passes the prescribed
-- test of competence to drive."
GIVEN `months suspended` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a new test is needed after the suspension` IF `months suspended` AT LEAST 12

§§ `35A -- revocation of a new driver's licence`

-- s 35A(1): the Deputy Commissioner "may revoke a driving licence if -- (a) within a period of 12 months from the date of the
-- grant of the licence, the record of the holder ... establishes that it would not be in the interests of public safety for him
-- or her to continue to hold the licence". (2) to (4) set up a points system with a "revocation threshold" in the same words as
-- s 45. (9): a person is a "new driver" from the grant "ending on the eve of the first anniversary of the grant".
-- (7A): if a licence is revoked when the person is a new driver in respect of it, "every other driving licence ... is deemed to be
-- revoked as well unless the person is then not a new driver in respect of that other driving licence."
-- Time is counted in whole days since the grant; day 0 is the day of grant; the eve of the first anniversary is taken as day 364
-- (INFERENCE: ignores leap years).
GIVEN `days since the grant` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a new driver` IF
    `days since the grant` AT LEAST 0 AND `days since the grant` LESS THAN 365

GIVEN `days since the grant` IS A NUMBER
      `points within the prescribed period` IS A NUMBER
      `the revocation threshold` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Deputy Commissioner may revoke on points` IF
        `is a new driver` `days since the grant`
    AND `points within the prescribed period` AT LEAST `the revocation threshold`

GIVEN `revoked while a new driver on this licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days since the grant of the other licence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the other licence falls with it` IF
        `revoked while a new driver on this licence`
    AND `is a new driver` `days since the grant of the other licence`

§§ `81(1B) -- the owner's presumption`

-- s 81(1B): where an owner who holds a driving licence is guilty under (1A) of failing to give information identifying the driver,
-- "and the driver ... is alleged or suspected to be guilty of an offence specified in Part 1 of the Third Schedule, the owner ...
-- is presumed, until the contrary is proved, to be driving the motor vehicle". Third Schedule Part 1 item 1 lists "Sections
-- 63(4), 65, ...". Speeding is on it.
GIVEN `the owner failed to identify the driver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner holds a driving licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is speeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner is presumed to have been driving` IF
        `the owner failed to identify the driver`
    AND `the owner holds a driving licence`
    AND `the offence is speeding`

§§ `The REQ-0273 question in one record`

-- The facts the Act needs, and the facts it leaves to the rules (marked RULES).
DECLARE SpeedingCase HAS
    `speed limit` IS A NUMBER
    `speed` IS A NUMBER
    `an earlier speeding conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `composition sum demanded` IS A NUMBER
    `points for this offence` IS A NUMBER
    `points already in the period` IS A NUMBER
    `suspension threshold` IS A NUMBER

-- RULES: `prescribed as compoundable`, `composition sum demanded`, `points for this offence`, `suspension threshold`.
GIVEN `the case` IS A SpeedingCase
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the case's maximum fine` MEANS `the maximum fine for speeding` (`the case`'s `an earlier speeding conviction`)

GIVEN `the case` IS A SpeedingCase
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the case's maximum months` MEANS `the maximum months of imprisonment for speeding` (`the case`'s `an earlier speeding conviction`)

GIVEN `the case` IS A SpeedingCase
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the case's composition cap` MEANS `the composition cap for speeding` (`the case`'s `an earlier speeding conviction`)

GIVEN `the case` IS A SpeedingCase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the case's composition sum is within the Act` IF
    `the composition sum is within the Act` (`the case`'s `composition sum demanded`) (`the case`'s `an earlier speeding conviction`) (`the case`'s `prescribed as compoundable`)

GIVEN `the case` IS A SpeedingCase
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the case's points total` MEANS `the case`'s `points already in the period` + `the case`'s `points for this offence`

GIVEN `the case` IS A SpeedingCase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the case's licence may be suspended` IF
        `the speeding offence is committed` (`the case`'s `speed limit`) (`the case`'s `speed`)
    AND `the Deputy Commissioner may suspend on points` (`the case's points total` `the case`) (`the case`'s `suspension threshold`)

GIVEN `the case` IS A SpeedingCase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the case counts towards a repeat dangerous driver` IF
    `the excess over the limit` (`the case`'s `speed limit`) (`the case`'s `speed`) GREATER THAN 40
